hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18223","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Murrah ibn Kab or Kab ibn Murrah al-Sulami, Shubah said: Mansur had narrated it to me mentioning three between him and Murrah ibn Kab, then he said afterward from Mansur from Salim from Murrah or from Kab, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which part of the night is most heard. He said: The last depth of the night."
"18224","Then he said: Prayer is accepted until you pray the morning prayer, then there is no prayer until the sun rises and becomes a spear length or two spear lengths, then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands like a spear, then there is no prayer until the sun declines, then prayer is accepted until you pray the afternoon prayer, then there is no prayer until the sun sets."
"18225","And when the servant performs ablution and washes his hands his sins fall from between his hands, and when he washes his face his sins fall from his face, and when he washes his forearms his sins fall from his forearms, and when he washes his feet his sins fall from his feet. Shubah said: And he did not mention wiping the head."
"18226","And any man who frees a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every limb of his limbs for a limb of his limbs, and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every two limbs of their limbs for a limb of his limbs, and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she will be her ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every limb of her limbs for a limb of her limbs."
"18227","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah, he said: When Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, preachers stood at Iliya, and the last of them to stand was a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Murrah ibn Kab, and he said: Were it not for a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would not have stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a trial, and I think he said and brought it near, Ismail doubted, then a veiled man passed, so he said: This and his companions on that day are upon the truth. So I went and took his shoulder and turned his face toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This. He said: Yes. He said: And it was Uthman, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
"18228","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, he said: A man said to Kab ibn Murrah or Murrah ibn Kab: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may your father be for Allah, and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who frees a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every bone of his bones for a bone of his bones, and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every two bones of their bones for a bone of his bones, and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she will be her ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every bone of her bones for a bone of her bones."
"18229","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar. He said: So I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah Almighty has aided you and given you and answered you, and your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them. So he turned away from him. He said: So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Allah Almighty has aided you and given you and answered you, and your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them. He said: O Allah, give us relieving, fertile, widespread, abundant rain, swift, beneficial without harm. And it was only a week or so until they were rained upon. Shubah said: In the supplication is a word I heard from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Salim about seeking rain, and in the hadith of Habib or Amr from Salim, he said: I came to you from people whose stallions show no vigor and whose shepherds carry no provisions."
"18230","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, he said: He said to Kab ibn Murrah: O Kab ibn Murrah, narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Shoot the people of Sana, whoever reaches the enemy with an arrow Allah will raise him a degree thereby. He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Nahham said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a degree. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed it is not your mother's step, but between two degrees is one hundred years."
"18231","He said: O Kab ibn Murrah, narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frees a Muslim person, it will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every bone of him for a bone of him, and whoever frees two Muslim women, they will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed with every two bones of them for a bone of him."
"18232","And whoever grows grey hair in the cause of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"18233","He said: O Kab ibn Murrah, narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the cause of Allah Almighty, it is like one who frees a slave."
"18234","And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and a man came to him and said: Seek rain from Allah for Mudar. He said: So he said: You are indeed bold, for Mudar. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you sought aid from Allah Almighty and He aided you, and you supplicated to Allah Almighty and He answered you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands saying: O Allah, give us relieving, fertile, wholesome, widespread, abundant rain, swift without delay, beneficial without harm. He said: So they were revived. He said: They did not remain but that they came to him complaining of much rain, saying: Houses have collapsed. He said: So he raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: So the clouds began breaking apart to the right and left."
"18235","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us from Sulaym ibn Amir from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: We were encamped with Muawiyah after the killing of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, when Kab ibn Murrah al-Bahzi stood and said: Were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would not have stood in this place. When he heard the mention of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he seated the people, then he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, passed by groomed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A trial will surely emerge from beneath the feet, or from between the legs, of this man, this one on that day and whoever follows him is upon guidance. He said: So Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi stood from beside the pulpit and said: You are indeed the companion of this. He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, I was indeed present in that gathering, and had I known I had one to confirm me in the army I would have been the first to speak of it."
"18236","Muhammad ibn Bakr that is al-Bursani narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid informed us, Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ashath, he said: Preachers stood at Iliya under the rule of Muawiyah, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and they spoke, and the last to speak was Murrah ibn Kab, and he said: Were it not for a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would not have stood. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention a trial and bring it near, then a masked man passed, so he said: This one on that day and his companions are upon truth and guidance. So I said: This one, O Messenger of Allah, turning his face toward him, and he said: This one, and it was Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him."
